Artificial Anasazi: baseline fixes with soil and crowding variants
==================================================================

This repository contains modified versions of the Artificial Anasazi model from
the NetLogo Models Library.

Original work
-------------
NetLogo Artificial Anasazi model.
Copyright 2010 Uri Wilensky.
Stonedahl, F. and Wilensky, U. (2010). NetLogo Artificial Anasazi model.
http://ccl.northwestern.edu/netlogo/models/ArtificialAnasazi
Center for Connected Learning and Computer-Based Modeling, Northwestern
University, Evanston, IL.
Licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike 3.0
License (see LICENSE). To inquire about commercial licenses for models from the
Models Library, contact netlogo-commercial-admin@ccl.northwestern.edu.

The model is a lightly adapted version of the NetLogo replication by Marco
Janssen (with help of Sean Bergin and Allen Lee) of the Artificial Anasazi model
by Jeffrey S. Dean, George J. Gumerman, Joshua M. Epstein, Robert Axtell, Alan C.
Swedlund, Miles Parker, and Steven McCarroll. The original model was written in
Ascape. Janssen's version is at
https://www.comses.net/codebases/2222/releases/1.1.0/

The files in data/ come with the Models Library model.

